      "label": "Amyloid Pathology"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tau Pathology and Neurofibrillary Tangle Formation",
      "description": "Hyperphosphorylation of tau proteins leads to the formation of neurofibrillary tangles inside neurons. These tangles destabilize microtubules, impair axonal transport, and ultimately result in cell death. Elevated levels of total tau (TAU) and phosphorylated tau (PTAU) in CSF are hallmark biomarkers in AD, indicating ongoing neurodegeneration and correlating with cognitive impairment.",
