      "name": "Neurodegeneration and Brain Atrophy",
      "description": "Progressive loss of neurons and synapses results in atrophy of specific brain regions implicated in AD. This includes early atrophy in the hippocampus and entorhinal cortex, as well as widespread atrophy in the temporal, parietal, and whole brain regions as disease advances. These structural changes, which are detectable by MRI measures like ventricular enlargement and decreased regional brain volumes, underpin clinical symptoms of memory loss and cognitive decline.",
