      "name": "Glucose Hypometabolism and Synaptic Dysfunction",
      "description": "Reduced neuronal and synaptic activity in the AD brain is observed as hypometabolism, particularly in temporoparietal and posterior cingulate cortices. This metabolic impairment is captured by FDG-PET imaging showing reduced glucose uptake and is closely associated with ongoing cognitive and functional decline in AD patients.",
